            <ArticleTitle>Congenital indifference to pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>755-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Congenital analgesia can vary from simple analgesia without any systemic dysfunction to more serious conditions associated with peripheral neuropathy, self-mutilation, and mental retardation. Prevention of injury is important for normal growth of the child.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
